    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\n`{ show_contents = true }` for `gen_clues.registers()` produces a lot of useless empty lines with a need to scroll through the window.\r\n\r\nit would be good to not show lines that are completely empty, or are only whitespace, so that only relevant registers are shown",
